Finding 015
Title
Observed Route Speed Shows a Stronger Relationship with NFL Career Usage Than Athleticism Score

Context
Following the route-specific skill framework proposed in Milestone 03, GO_ROUTE_RIGHT was selected as the primary drill for evaluating straight-line speed.

The objective was to determine whether tracking-derived speed metrics show meaningful relationships with NFL career outcomes.

Drill
GO_ROUTE_RIGHT
Sample:

104 route attempts
Metrics Evaluated
Tracking Metrics:

burst_mean
avg_acceleration_mean
max_acceleration_mean
max_speed_mean
Traditional Metrics:

NGS Athleticism Score
Forty Yard Dash
NFL Outcomes:

career_games_started
career_offensive_snaps
Results
Relationship with NFL Career Games Started
max_speed_mean ↔ career_games_started

r = 0.313
ngs_athleticism_score ↔ career_games_started

r = 0.235
burst_mean ↔ career_games_started

r = -0.023
max_acceleration_mean ↔ career_games_started

r = 0.270
Relationship with Athleticism Score
max_speed_mean ↔ ngs_athleticism_score

r = 0.321
Interpretation:

Observed route speed and athleticism score appear related but are not measuring the same underlying characteristic.

Additional Validation
