Observation:

Players in the upper speed quintiles accumulated substantially more career starts and offensive snaps than players in the lower speed quintiles.

Interpretation
Among all route-derived metrics evaluated so far, observed maximum speed demonstrated the strongest and most consistent relationship with NFL career usage.

The relationship appears stronger than that observed for the NGS Athleticism Score within this sample.

While the observed correlations remain moderate, the quintile analysis provides additional evidence that directly measured route speed may be a meaningful indicator of future NFL participation.

Limitations
Analysis limited to GO_ROUTE_RIGHT.
Sample size remains modest.
NFL career outcomes are influenced by many factors beyond athletic ability.
Correlation does not imply causation.
Findings require validation on additional speed-oriented drills.
Next Steps
Replicate analysis on other route drills.
Validate whether speed remains the strongest skill dimension.
Compare speed metrics against draft capital.
Evaluate whether observed route speed provides incremental value over traditional combine metrics.
